audience: Maintainers and decision-makers evaluating adoption
purpose: What did the 2026-09-09 experiment measure about document check cost and detection?

docs/reports/2026-09-09-adoption-cost.md is the 2026-09-09 experiment report; its conclusion is that the bundled document checks dropped from a median 8.95 s to 4.14 s and the paired additional delay from 8.17 s to 3.32 s, meeting the 5 s criterion, and that this is execution cost only, not human productivity.
Translated from Korean in full: conclusion and applicability, method and conditions, results table (all values and units kept), the attribution to check-structure.sh, the 1,815 to 1,070 line entry-file note, raw data links, limitations and follow-up.
Historical facts were not updated to the current implementation; "Experiment conditions" became "Method and conditions" so the case-sensitive pattern matches.
No Korean literals retained; the native command stays as inline code.
Compared against HEAD; no numbers, conditions or limitations dropped. Limitation: self-review by the translator.

